<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">(b) </span>Evaluation accuracy.</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>
Evaluation of RSI with MASS.
(a) Cumulative number of tasks for which a workflow is unanimously preferred to the baseline by external strong LLM judges.
(b) Task-solving performance across model generations on eight synthetic training tasks, three synthetic test tasks, and two research benchmarks.
(c) Evaluator agreement with external strong-model judges.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">MASS completes the recursive process <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}\rightarrow{\mathcal{L}}^{(1)}\rightarrow{\mathcal{L}}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}\rightarrow{\mathcal{L}}^{(1)}\rightarrow{\mathcal{L}}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> in our experiments.
Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4.2 Main results: improvement across model roles ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Recursive Self-Improvement through Multi-Agent Self-Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> summarizes performance across the model’s
three roles. First, Figure <a href="#S4.T1.st1" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 4.2 Main results: improvement across model roles ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Recursive Self-Improvement through Multi-Agent Self-Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1(a)</span></a> compares <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(g)}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(g)}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Performance improves on ScienceAgentBench from <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="28.7\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>28.7</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">28.7\%</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="31.8\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>31.8</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">31.8\%</annotation></semantics></math>, on MLR-Bench from <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.58" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.58</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.58</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.40</annotation></semantics></math>, on AstaBench from <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.053" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.053</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.053</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.067" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.067</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.067</annotation></semantics></math>, and on DSBench from <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.473" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.473</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.473</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.482" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.482</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.482</annotation></semantics></math>. Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Recursive Self-Improvement through Multi-Agent Self-Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> further compares score per output token: on these four research benchmarks, <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.6\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.6\times</annotation></semantics></math> higher score per output token than <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>. On the three test tasks, <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves a <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="53.9\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>53.9</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">53.9\%</annotation></semantics></math> win rate against <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> reaches <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="69.9\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>69.9</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">69.9\%</annotation></semantics></math>. Directly comparing successive generations, <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> also shows a larger gain over <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, with a <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60.8\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>60.8</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60.8\%</annotation></semantics></math> win rate, compared with the <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="53.9\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>53.9</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">53.9\%</annotation></semantics></math> win rate of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These increasing gains may be partly explained by natural improvements in the
optimizer and evaluator across <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}\rightarrow{\mathcal{L}}^{(1)}\rightarrow{\mathcal{L}}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}\rightarrow{\mathcal{L}}^{(1)}\rightarrow{\mathcal{L}}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that post-training was only on task-solving traces.
Figure <a href="#S4.F3.sf1" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 4.2 Main results: improvement across model roles ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Recursive Self-Improvement through Multi-Agent Self-Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(a)</span></a> compares <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(g)}(x_{t}\oplus w_{t}^{(g,i)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(g)}(x_{t}\oplus w_{t}^{(g,i)})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> across workflow iterations <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[10]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[10]</annotation></semantics></math> and MASS generations <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\{0,1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\{0,1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>, showing that post-trained models discover successful workflows earlier.
Figure <a href="#S4.T1.st2" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 4.2 Main results: improvement across model roles ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Recursive Self-Improvement through Multi-Agent Self-Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1(b)</span></a> measures agreement between the self-evaluator <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(g)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(g)}</annotation></semantics></math> and the external reference judgments. The agreement increases from <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.73" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.73</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.73</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.91" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.91</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.91</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.93" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.93</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.93</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Together, these results support transfer from task-solving
self-supervision to workflow optimization and self-evaluation without
separate training targets for those roles.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table" style="width:47%;">
<table id="S4.T1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">Executor <math id="S4.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\text{agent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>agent</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\text{agent}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S4.T1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">Comparator <math id="S4.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\text{agent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>agent</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\text{agent}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S4.T1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">
<span id="S4.T1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S4.T1.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_right">Win rate</span>
</span></th></tr>
