<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Per-task comparison of <math id="A3.T5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> with the no-harness base.
Both models receive the bare task prompt. Each task has ten
index-matched rollout pairs, assessed by two reporting judges with three
seeds each, yielding 60 verdicts per task. Wins, losses, and ties
are counted from the student’s perspective; win share is
<math id="A3.T5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W/(W+L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W/(W+L)</annotation></semantics></math>. Loop-detection halts remain in the evaluation.
Task descriptions are given in Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ B.1 Tasks, teacher collection, and validation ‣ Appendix B Training data and optimization ‣ Recursive Self-Improvement through Multi-Agent Self-Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.T6" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
