<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 12: </span>Task-information estimates <math id="A6.T12.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{I}(Z_{c};T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{I}(Z_{c};T)</annotation></semantics></math> (nats)
along the crown path. In all four encoder/estimator configurations,
roles and instructions decrease while contracts and hops increase
between <math id="A6.T12.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.T12.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=11</annotation></semantics></math> (arrows). Unadjusted estimates use the full
sample; permutation-adjusted estimates subtract a shuffled baseline
using 43-agent samples (Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Workflow-information estimates ‣ Recursive Self-Improvement through Multi-Agent Self-Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>).</figcaption>
</figure>
